---
name: ufw
description: |
  VM-level inbound firewall management using the packaged ufw frontend (own
  package, no dependency on stemcell-shipped ufw). Applies a declarative list
  of inbound allow rules over a default-deny-incoming / default-allow-outgoing
  posture, plus a mandatory operational allow baseline (SSH, monitoring
  scrape, other inbound management endpoints) that rules cannot remove.
  Egress-aware by design: in NATS mode the BOSH agent, health monitor and
  blobstore are agent-initiated outbound connections, so they require no
  inbound allow. Designed to be
  delivered fleet-wide through runtime-config addons, one addon per exposed
  protocol, scoped with include.jobs.

  Modes:
  - enforce=false (default): the desired rule set is rendered and logged for
    review, the host firewall is left untouched (rollout dry-run).
  - stay_armed_on_stop=true (default): stopping/unmonitoring the job keeps the
    applied rules active; reboot persistence is provided by monit re-running
    the apply at boot. Set false for debug disarming.

  The job owns only the rules it tagged in comments ('paas-ufw/<instance
  group>'); manually added ufw rules and other firewall tooling are never
  touched. Rendering fails (deploy aborts, firewall untouched) on invalid
  CIDRs/ports or missing baseline CIDRs.
packages:
- ufw
templates:
  ufw.json.erb: config/ufw.json
  ufw-cli.erb: bin/ufw
  pre-start.erb: bin/pre-start
  start.erb: bin/start
  stop.erb: bin/stop
  monit_check.erb: bin/monit_check
  ctl.erb: bin/ctl
consumes: []
properties:
  ufw.rules:
    description: |
      Inbound allow rules. List of {description, from, to_ports, protocol}:
      from: list of source CIDRs (e.g. 10.20.30.0/24, fe80::/64),
      to_ports: list of ports or ranges (integer or "3306:3308"),
      protocol: tcp | udp | tcp/udp.
      Rendered as: ufw allow from <cidr> to any port <port> proto <protocol>
    default: []
    example:
    - description: mysql from apps subnet
      from: ["10.20.30.0/24"]
      to_ports: [3306]
      protocol: tcp
  ufw.allow_bosh:
    description: |
      Mandatory operational allow baseline, always applied before ufw.rules
      and impossible to override: source CIDRs for the *inbound* operational
      endpoints only — SSH (22) from jumpbox/operators, and the monitoring
      scrape endpoint (node exporter on its environment port, e.g. 9099 when
      a runtime-config addon overrides the 9100 default; add 8844/tcp only
      if bosh-dns health-server checks reach this VM). Do NOT add BOSH
      control-plane ports here: in NATS mode the agent dials out to
      nats://director:4222 and pulls blobs from the director blobstore, so
      agent/HM/blobstore traffic is egress and needs no inbound rule
      (default-deny incoming leaves egress untouched). No default on
      purpose: rendering FAILS when empty, so a forgotten addon property
      aborts the deploy instead of locking operators out of their VMs.
      Same entry shape as ufw.rules.
    example:
    - description: ssh from jumpbox
      from: ["10.0.4.50/32"]
      to_ports: [22]
      protocol: tcp
    - description: node exporter scrape from monitoring
      from: ["10.0.20.0/24"]
      to_ports: [9099]
      protocol: tcp
  ufw.enforce:
    description: "false: render and report the desired rules without touching the firewall (dry-run). true: activate them."
    default: false
  ufw.stay_armed_on_stop:
    description: "true: keep rules armed when the job stops (default, survives reboots via monit). false: ufw disable on stop (debug escape hatch)."
    default: true
  ufw.logging:
    description: "ufw logging level: low | medium | high | full | off"
    default: low
  ufw.ipv6:
    description: "Manage ip6tables alongside iptables. BOSH stemcell/IaaS networking is IPv4-only: off by default, opt-in"
    default: false
